\* Shen sequent-calculus specification — edit this file to define your
   domain invariants. Generated by `sb init --lang elixir`.

   `sb gen` lowers each datatype to an @opaque Elixir struct whose new/N
   checks every `: verified` premise; `sb mutate-spec` requires a hostile
   program in specs/hostile/ for each premise. *\

\* Wrapper: a domain string, no validation. Single-line (right-only) rule:
   the double-line form also adds a left rule (account-id → string) that
   sends Shen's search past its inference budget once two account-ids
   meet in one premise. *\
(datatype account-id
  X : string;
  ______________
  X : account-id;)

\* Constrained: a validated number *\
(datatype amount
  X : number;
  (>= X 0) : verified;
  ====================
  X : amount;)

\* Guarded composite: a cross-field invariant *\
(datatype transfer
  From : account-id;
  To : account-id;
  Amt : amount;
  (not (= From To)) : verified;
  ==============================
  [From To Amt] : transfer;)

\* A pure function for `sb derive` ([[derive.specs]] with lang = "elixir") *\
(define within-limit?
  {number --> number --> boolean}
  Amt Limit -> (<= Amt Limit))
